### `man_1_simple_shell` (Student style)

```groff
.TH HSH 1 "September 2026" "Holberton School" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hsh \- simple UNIX command line interpreter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./hsh
.SH DESCRIPTION
hsh is a simple shell written in C for the Holberton School project.
.PP
It reads commands from the user (or from a pipe/file), finds the program
using the PATH, and executes it in a child process.
.PP
It works in both interactive and non-interactive modes.
.SH FEATURES
.IP \(bu 2
Shows a prompt ($ ) in interactive mode
.IP \(bu 2
Can execute commands with arguments
.IP \(bu 2
Uses the PATH to find commands
.IP \(bu 2
Supports absolute and relative paths
.IP \(bu 2
Has two built-in commands: exit and env
.IP \(bu 2
Handles Ctrl+D (EOF)
.SH BUILT-IN COMMANDS
.TP
.B exit
Exits the shell
.TP
.B env
Prints all environment variables
.SH HOW TO USE
.SS Interactive mode
.PP
.nf
$ ./hsh
$ ls
$ pwd
$ ls -l /tmp
$ env
$ exit
.fi
.SS Non-interactive mode
.PP
.nf
$ echo "ls" | ./hsh
$ echo "ls -l" | ./hsh
$ cat commands.txt | ./hsh
.fi
.SH ERRORS
If the command does not exist, the shell prints:
.PP
.nf
./hsh: 1: command: not found
.fi
.PP
and returns the status 127.
.SH LIMITATIONS
This shell does not support:
.IP \(bu 2
Pipes (|)
.IP \(bu 2
Redirections (>, <)
.IP \(bu 2
Command separators (;)
.IP \(bu 2
Logical operators (&&, ||)
.IP \(bu 2
Quotes or escaping
.IP \(bu 2
Background jobs (&)
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
$ ./hsh
$ /bin/ls
$ ls -la
$ env
$ exit
.fi
.PP
.nf
$ echo "pwd" | ./hsh
$ printf "ls\\nenv\\nexit\\n" | ./hsh
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
sh(1), bash(1), fork(2), execve(2), wait(2)
.SH AUTHORS
See the AUTHORS file.
.SH BUGS
This is a simple educational shell. It does not have all the features of a real shell like bash.
